WEBVTT

00:01.790 --> 00:06.530
<i>There once was a powerless prince who 
saved a kingdom with his tiny courage.</i>

00:07.660 --> 00:10.110
<i>The courage to face challenges...</i>

00:10.110 --> 00:12.060
<i>The courage to never give up...</i>

00:12.470 --> 00:14.650
<i>The courage to trust others...</i>

00:15.500 --> 00:20.180
<i>A treasure chest of untold courage 
is now about to be opened.</i>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.550
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

00:27.130 --> 00:33.550
<b>— The Treasure Chest of Courage —</b>

00:36.500 --> 00:41.260
<i>The callous absurdity I've 
carried with me since birth</i>

00:41.260 --> 00:46.930
<i>meant playing shadow tag to find my next meal</i>

00:47.480 --> 00:50.690
<i>Bit by bit, my heart got bent out of shape</i>

00:50.690 --> 00:53.710
<i>until I tuned out both 
the cheers and the jeers</i>

00:55.910 --> 01:00.580
<i>That's how I survived my initial loneliness</i>

01:00.580 --> 01:05.590
<i>Night falls and the darkness grows</i>

01:06.000 --> 01:10.810
<i>blending in, coalescing</i>

01:11.120 --> 01:15.570
<i>around so trivial a fate as my own</i>

01:15.570 --> 01:18.380
<i>Hey, I want to get through to you</i>

01:18.380 --> 01:22.420
<i>though I may only know commonplace words</i>

01:23.930 --> 01:26.740
<i>It's so frustrating having to be like this</i>

01:26.740 --> 01:29.670
<i>Hey, never mind that it may not be easy</i>

01:29.670 --> 01:34.080
<i>to become angry or let yourself cry</i>

01:35.190 --> 01:38.770
<i>because someone could be listening in</i>

01:38.770 --> 01:41.990
<i>The only thing that's 
certain is the temperature</i>

01:44.250 --> 01:49.170
<i>whether or not we can speak heart to heart</i>

01:52.520 --> 01:53.720
<i>Following the death of Satun,</i>

01:54.330 --> 01:57.320
<i>Desha and Despa began searching 
in secret for the demon,</i>

01:57.320 --> 02:01.350
<i>so that they could lift the curse 
of immortality from Ouken.</i>

02:02.490 --> 02:08.070
<i>However, Ouken's brothers were not the 
only ones who wanted to save him.</i>

02:05.810 --> 02:09.770
<b>The Law of the Underworld</b>

02:08.270 --> 02:09.770
What did you want to speak about?

02:10.120 --> 02:13.760
I'd like you to allow me to 
help search for the demon.

02:13.760 --> 02:15.700
Oh, so you've heard?

02:17.490 --> 02:20.350
It says that in order to lift 
Ouken's curse of immortality,

02:20.350 --> 02:22.860
we will need the head of a demon.

02:22.860 --> 02:25.430
A demon? Where do we find one?

02:25.430 --> 02:26.620
I don't know.

02:27.280 --> 02:29.260
I'll send out the troops and have them look.

02:29.260 --> 02:31.320
Ouken, it will be all right.

02:31.320 --> 02:33.220
I'm sure you'll get over this.

02:35.460 --> 02:38.670
I owe a great deal to Prince Ouken.

02:39.010 --> 02:40.620
I would like to help.

02:40.920 --> 02:46.350
You can't. As a monster, you are not 
allowed to leave the underworld.

02:46.350 --> 02:47.470
But sire...

02:47.470 --> 02:51.510
That is the law. I cannot permit it,
 no matter the reason.

02:54.310 --> 02:55.790
Cheers!

02:55.280 --> 02:57.200
Cheers!

03:01.530 --> 03:03.950
There's nothing better than 
a drink after training!

03:04.220 --> 03:05.390
Nothing better!

03:05.390 --> 03:06.530
So good!

03:06.530 --> 03:09.570
It really hits the spot!

03:09.570 --> 03:12.130
It's been so long since we 
all had a drink together.

03:12.130 --> 03:13.720
Has it?

03:13.720 --> 03:15.400
How about another round?

03:15.400 --> 03:16.950
Hey, Mr. Second-in-Command.

03:16.950 --> 03:18.450
Sorry I'm late.

03:18.710 --> 03:20.370
Today, drinks are on me.

03:20.370 --> 03:21.630
You mean it?!

03:21.630 --> 03:24.960
Yay! Keep the food and drinks coming!

03:24.960 --> 03:27.100
Hey you, show a little restraint.

03:27.100 --> 03:28.430
Oh, where's the harm?

03:28.430 --> 03:29.740
It's all right.

03:29.740 --> 03:30.920
Thanks!

03:30.920 --> 03:33.700
It's so rare for you to buy us drinks.

03:33.700 --> 03:34.990
Well, the occasion is right.

03:35.340 --> 03:40.880
So I told him, "If you value your 
life, you'd better get outta here!"

03:37.930 --> 03:39.990
Ha ha! Don't drink too much, now.

03:41.740 --> 03:44.430
We may have overdone it last night.

03:44.430 --> 03:48.300
Damned if Fren didn't 
just up and leave, too.

03:48.300 --> 03:51.570
Still, it was nice of him to 
spend so much coin on us.

03:50.860 --> 03:51.830
Hurry!

03:51.830 --> 03:53.090
Check his room!

03:53.670 --> 03:55.030
What's all the fuss about?

03:55.030 --> 03:56.560
What's happened?

03:57.230 --> 04:00.060
Fren, second-in-command of the 
Order of the Underworld,

04:00.060 --> 04:01.870
has fled the underworld.

04:01.870 --> 04:04.920
In accordance with the law, 
I'm ordering his execution.

04:05.830 --> 04:06.650
Yes, sire.

04:08.260 --> 04:09.660
Fren did?

04:09.660 --> 04:12.510
Is Fren gonna be killed?

04:12.510 --> 04:14.650
Why would he run away?

04:14.650 --> 04:18.280
There's no way he'd break the 
law without a good reason.

04:18.280 --> 04:20.070
Something must have happened.

04:29.940 --> 04:31.750
Prince Despa!

04:35.840 --> 04:37.460
Prince Despa!

04:37.730 --> 04:39.300
Prince Despa?

04:40.530 --> 04:44.480
What is it? I am very busy right now!

04:44.480 --> 04:46.520
Well, there was something 
we needed to ask you—

04:46.520 --> 04:48.810
I told you, I'm busy—

04:51.900 --> 04:54.370
Prince Ouken has become immortal?

04:54.370 --> 04:55.270
Yes.

04:55.920 --> 04:59.510
Word is that Fren said he wanted 
to help search for the demon,

04:59.510 --> 05:01.860
but Brother would not grant him permission.

05:02.260 --> 05:06.090
So then he... Fren has 
been by his side forever.

05:06.090 --> 05:08.820
Would you please share your wisdom with us?

05:09.170 --> 05:10.520
Hmm...

05:10.520 --> 05:11.850
Please!

05:11.850 --> 05:15.450
Fren is the kind of man who would put 
his life on the line for Prince Ouken.

05:15.450 --> 05:17.390
For Prince Ouken's sake, too!

05:17.390 --> 05:18.790
Prince Despa!

05:19.240 --> 05:22.010
Hmm, very well.

05:22.610 --> 05:24.310
Thank you very much!

05:24.310 --> 05:28.010
However, make absolutely sure 
not to bring my name into this.

05:28.010 --> 05:28.580
Huh?

05:28.580 --> 05:32.030
I'm not keen on taking part of 
the fall for whatever happens.

05:32.030 --> 05:33.900
Huh?

05:35.910 --> 05:38.850
We heard that Fren went into 
a town on the surface.

05:38.850 --> 05:41.970
That's where we'll settle this. 
Everyone, brace yourselves.

05:41.970 --> 05:42.640
Yes, sir!

05:42.990 --> 05:45.620
Still, I feel so heavyhearted...

05:49.770 --> 05:51.660
Say your prayers!

05:52.660 --> 05:53.580
Brigands?!

05:57.360 --> 05:59.610
What are you waiting for?! 
Seize them at once!

06:00.860 --> 06:02.610
I think it's time for us to scram!

06:02.610 --> 06:03.430
Yeah!

06:03.430 --> 06:04.660
Don't let them escape!

06:04.660 --> 06:05.640
Yes, sir!

06:07.020 --> 06:10.290
Why would they possibly attack the Order?

06:15.540 --> 06:16.420
Where are the brigands?

06:16.420 --> 06:19.880
They got away from us, sir. 
We are terribly sorry.

06:19.880 --> 06:22.670
They could be in league 
with Fren. Stay on your toes.

06:22.670 --> 06:23.370
Yes, sir!

06:23.640 --> 06:26.720
Word has it that Fren is moving 
on to the next town. Let's hurry.

06:26.720 --> 06:27.560
Right!

06:30.170 --> 06:35.910
Demon? I've heard stories about one, 
but I'm not sure it really exists.

06:37.230 --> 06:40.260
I see. Let me have that sword.

06:40.720 --> 06:41.720
You got it.

06:48.660 --> 06:49.440
Tch...

06:49.440 --> 06:50.290
There he is!

06:50.850 --> 06:51.820
Seize him!

06:51.820 --> 06:52.640
Yes, sir!

07:11.500 --> 07:12.980
Fren, run!

07:13.510 --> 07:14.690
Aban...

07:16.270 --> 07:18.160
You're not getting past us!

07:20.670 --> 07:23.850
So you really are Fren's pals after all.

07:24.130 --> 07:25.180
Slay them!

07:38.460 --> 07:39.600
Fren?!

07:39.600 --> 07:40.840
I'm fighting, too!

07:40.840 --> 07:42.110
Run away, you dumbass!

07:42.110 --> 07:43.560
How am I supposed to do that?!

07:43.880 --> 07:48.160
Fren, you scoundrel! You, a monster, 
dare to leave the underworld?!

07:48.160 --> 07:51.290
In accordance with the law, 
you are to be executed!

08:05.790 --> 08:06.530
Fren!

08:12.890 --> 08:14.190
Damn it!

08:13.430 --> 08:14.710
Run!

08:15.700 --> 08:16.770
Let them go!

08:16.770 --> 08:18.060
But sir...

08:18.060 --> 08:20.990
We accomplished our mission to execute Fren.

08:30.890 --> 08:31.980
We're going home.

08:36.030 --> 08:37.360
Worked like a charm.

08:37.360 --> 08:38.690
Oh, yeah!

08:38.690 --> 08:40.650
What exactly just happened?

08:40.650 --> 08:44.920
We wanted to help you, so we had 
the captain stage all of this.

08:45.300 --> 08:48.370
I'm surprised someone as uptight 
as him went along with it.

08:48.640 --> 08:50.100
Yeah, well...

08:51.010 --> 08:54.490
Aban? What are you doing here?

08:55.280 --> 08:59.420
Captain, please, call off Fren's execution.

08:59.420 --> 09:03.170
The reason Fren ran off was 
to help save Prince Ouken.

09:03.170 --> 09:06.010
Huh? How do you know about that?

09:07.480 --> 09:11.210
I heard you were at the tavern 
with Fren last night.

09:11.210 --> 09:14.640
If you're mixed up in all of this,
 I can't just overlook it.

09:14.640 --> 09:18.230
I'm begging you! We're doing 
all of this for Prince Ouken!

09:18.570 --> 09:19.700
Still...

09:19.970 --> 09:23.620
I was instructed to come 
here by Prince Despa.

09:23.990 --> 09:25.270
Prince Despa?!

09:25.270 --> 09:27.390
Yes. So please...

09:29.390 --> 09:33.620
Yeah, but Prince Despa said not 
to bring his name into it.

09:33.900 --> 09:35.540
Why would you go this far?

09:35.540 --> 09:39.160
Heh, we're just paying you 
back for the free drinks.

09:39.160 --> 09:41.940
Seriously, those were 
some expensive free drinks.

09:41.940 --> 09:44.660
Now I wish we'd have drunk even more!

09:46.220 --> 09:50.290
Fren, this is pretty much all we can do.

09:52.740 --> 09:55.410
Now I'll have to make sure 
to help Prince Ouken,

09:55.410 --> 09:59.010
so that I can repay my debt to you, too.

10:37.620 --> 10:39.770
Where in the world is this demon?

10:47.670 --> 10:48.740
Fren?

10:57.900 --> 11:01.400
The single lead I found 
to saving Prince Ouken

11:01.400 --> 11:03.690
is a woman that underwent the demon's curse.

11:04.220 --> 11:08.180
And I've learned that this woman is 
currently in the Kingdom of Bosse.

11:09.600 --> 11:13.350
I thought about going on ahead 
into the Kingdom of Bosse, but...

11:13.350 --> 11:18.770
No, coming back here was the 
wise decision. Nice work.

11:19.500 --> 11:21.370
I appreciate you saying so.

11:21.370 --> 11:23.330
What are you going to do now?

11:23.920 --> 11:27.800
I'm planning to personally take 
responsibility for breaking the law.

11:27.800 --> 11:28.990
Is that right?

11:30.400 --> 11:32.480
The accused will step forward.

11:33.930 --> 11:35.150
Silence.

11:36.950 --> 11:37.850
What's your name?

11:38.230 --> 11:41.260
Fren, second-in-command of the 
Order of the Underground.

11:41.680 --> 11:44.470
Fren is supposed to have been executed.

11:44.470 --> 11:45.190
Yes, sire.

11:45.710 --> 11:49.970
Many who were there witnessed it,
 including my own men.

11:49.970 --> 11:52.210
In other words, this man...

11:52.770 --> 11:56.450
is a miscreant who has 
falsely taken Fren's name.

11:58.740 --> 12:02.140
Henceforth, you are forbidden to 
enter the towns of the underworld.

12:02.660 --> 12:04.440
Away with you, at once.

12:20.770 --> 12:24.520
That was quite a fine judgment. 
Very unlike you, Brother.

12:24.950 --> 12:28.720
Hmph. I will do whatever 
it takes to help Ouken.

12:29.200 --> 12:30.030
Yes.

12:51.870 --> 12:56.880
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

12:57.930 --> 13:00.300
<i>When Despa stopped serving at the castle,</i>

13:00.300 --> 13:02.580
<i>he returned his beloved steed, 
Whiteking, to the state.</i>

13:03.140 --> 13:09.300
<i>But just in case, Despa entrusted the 
captain with caring for Whiteking.</i>

13:09.300 --> 13:14.310
<b>A White Horse in Love</b>

13:09.550 --> 13:12.410
You've put on some weight 
lately, haven't you?

13:12.410 --> 13:15.810
Yeah, I have. My belt's been getting tighter.

13:16.220 --> 13:19.790
But I still can't compete 
with Prince Despa's horse.

13:21.610 --> 13:23.510
What kind of competition is that?!

13:23.510 --> 13:24.420
Ah!

13:25.990 --> 13:27.220
Captain?

13:27.220 --> 13:28.810
Is something the matter?

13:29.920 --> 13:32.130
I-I forgot...

13:37.050 --> 13:41.530
Prince Despa entrusted me with 
her care. How could I let this happen?!

13:42.070 --> 13:45.600
Whiteking, we're going to get 
your beautiful form back!

13:49.930 --> 13:52.680
This is all the grass you're 
allowed to eat today.

13:59.020 --> 14:02.330
Exercise is best for slimming down. Go!

14:02.780 --> 14:03.620
Hey!

14:03.620 --> 14:04.900
Whoa!

14:10.330 --> 14:13.980
I'll make you run, even if I 
have to force you! Come on!

14:22.720 --> 14:27.240
You're going to make Prince Despa 
disgusted with you, looking like this.

14:29.310 --> 14:30.940
What is it, Whiteking?

14:38.760 --> 14:44.720
He seems to go in for good-looking horses.
 But the way you look now...

15:04.570 --> 15:06.180
Let's go, Whiteking!

15:07.640 --> 15:09.300
Hang in there, Whiteking!

15:12.850 --> 15:17.470
What's wrong, Whiteking?!

15:30.150 --> 15:34.040
Mm-hmm, you're the finest 
horse in the underworld.

15:52.820 --> 15:54.670
Wh-Whiteking...

16:04.260 --> 16:06.920
I-I wasn't trying to trick you!

16:10.180 --> 16:13.570
<i>Whiteking is back to her 
former beautiful form.</i>

16:13.980 --> 16:15.840
<i>And that is enough.</i>

16:20.450 --> 16:23.120
If we are to go to the 
faraway Kingdom of Bosse,

16:23.120 --> 16:26.150
then any mount other than 
Whiteking would be unthinkable.

16:26.150 --> 16:28.460
So, where is Whiteking?

16:29.080 --> 16:30.710
Over there.

16:34.930 --> 16:35.010
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

16:35.010 --> 16:35.090
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

16:35.090 --> 16:35.220
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

16:35.220 --> 16:39.930
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

16:41.850 --> 16:44.580
<i>After losing his mother, 
Hokuro was overcome with grief.</i>

16:44.990 --> 16:47.680
<i>There to show his concern for Hokuro</i>

16:47.680 --> 16:53.320
<i>was the young Bojji, who had similarly 
lost his mother, the late Queen Shiina.</i>

16:53.320 --> 16:58.780
<b>The Gentle Soldier, Hokuro</b>

16:53.690 --> 16:56.040
<i>I want to keep Prince Bojji safe.</i>

16:56.040 --> 16:58.780
<i>That is what I had in mind 
when I became a soldier.</i>

17:00.380 --> 17:02.620
<i>Whoa, this is huge.</i>

17:03.070 --> 17:05.490
<i>I guess the king is a giant, after all.</i>

17:07.380 --> 17:08.630
Excuse me...

17:08.630 --> 17:09.950
What is it, recruit?

17:10.300 --> 17:12.210
Where is Prince Bojji?

17:13.170 --> 17:15.980
The prince doesn't come 
out in public very often.

17:16.580 --> 17:18.690
I think he prefers to avoid others.

17:18.690 --> 17:20.530
He avoids others?

17:20.530 --> 17:23.520
Well, it's probably more 
to do with his deafness.

17:26.690 --> 17:31.470
<i>Yeah, that figures. It's not like 
it would be that easy to see him.</i>

17:36.530 --> 17:38.210
<i>It's Prince Bojji!</i>

17:38.210 --> 17:39.270
Hey, keep up!

17:39.270 --> 17:40.300
R-Right!

17:48.150 --> 17:52.070
"How... are... you?"

18:06.760 --> 18:07.850
Prince Bojji—

18:18.350 --> 18:22.570
I heard King Bosse passed away. 
The funeral is tomorrow.

18:22.570 --> 18:23.710
Yeah.

18:23.710 --> 18:26.510
So Prince Bojji will be the next king.

18:27.060 --> 18:28.480
That won't be a problem.

18:28.840 --> 18:31.330
Ha, you're pretty nonchalant.

18:32.250 --> 18:34.840
<i>I'm going to have Prince Bojji's back.</i>

18:36.870 --> 18:39.150
King Daida!

18:41.300 --> 18:43.680
King Daida!

19:02.530 --> 19:05.370
Do I have any volunteers?

19:05.370 --> 19:07.220
Like anyone would go.

19:09.650 --> 19:11.610
Prince Bojji is going on a journey,

19:11.610 --> 19:13.780
so they're picking a soldier to go with him.

19:15.300 --> 19:17.800
Me! I'd like to go!

19:35.610 --> 19:38.690
You'll never serve as a bodyguard 
with skills like that.

19:38.690 --> 19:42.570
I can cook, too! And take care 
of the prince's needs, as well!

19:42.570 --> 19:44.160
I'm sure I can be helpful!

19:44.160 --> 19:44.870
Enough!

19:47.270 --> 19:48.410
Queen Hiling,

19:49.010 --> 19:51.290
I can escort the prince myself.

19:51.640 --> 19:52.630
I see.

19:53.410 --> 19:56.960
Well, with one of the Big Four along, 
there shouldn't be any problem.

19:56.960 --> 20:00.910
No, madam. Now, I need to 
go get ready to leave.

20:01.270 --> 20:02.650
Please do.

20:02.970 --> 20:04.340
Please wait!

20:07.150 --> 20:09.650
Please hear me out!

20:10.870 --> 20:15.410
When I lost my mother, it was 
Prince Bojji who comforted me

20:15.410 --> 20:16.790
when I was crying.

20:16.790 --> 20:18.860
You know sign language?

20:19.360 --> 20:20.760
Ever since then,

20:21.090 --> 20:22.140
I've always...

20:22.940 --> 20:26.690
dreamed of working side-by-side 
with Prince Bojji!

20:27.980 --> 20:31.580
Please, allow me to accompany Prince Bojji!

20:33.040 --> 20:35.540
It's no use trying to play on our sympathy.

20:35.820 --> 20:37.440
I can escort the prince alone—

20:37.440 --> 20:40.500
I appoint this man to escort Bojji.

20:42.460 --> 20:43.740
But...

20:43.740 --> 20:45.290
That is an order.

20:46.130 --> 20:47.740
Very well.

20:47.740 --> 20:49.100
Hokuro, was it?

20:49.100 --> 20:49.800
Yes, sir!

20:50.160 --> 20:53.960
Make sure to do all in your 
power not to slow us down.

20:53.960 --> 20:54.700
Yes, sir!

21:20.380 --> 21:32.390
<i>Your precious words are now 
fluttering through the sky</i>

21:35.690 --> 21:41.400
<i>The nights when I was alone 
still had countless stars</i>

21:41.400 --> 21:46.530
<i>Even now, they're close at 
hand whenever I close my eyes</i>

21:47.030 --> 21:50.030
<i>With no destination, I kept on walking</i>

21:50.030 --> 21:52.870
<i>Although I was tired, I kept on walking</i>

21:52.870 --> 21:58.540
<i>I just wanted to remain in prayers forever</i>

21:58.540 --> 22:01.460
<i>Covered in scars, covered in mud</i>

22:01.460 --> 22:04.260
<i>stretching out hands that won't reach</i>

22:04.260 --> 22:14.060
<i>I want to seize a fragment of my 
hopes and dreams right this minute</i>

22:14.480 --> 22:20.230
<i>Keep smiling, keep smiling, 
you don't have to be strong</i>

22:20.230 --> 22:27.660
<i>That sweet smile, that 
sweet smile is all you need</i>

22:27.660 --> 22:32.240
<i>Your unique smile brings 
the power and strength</i>

22:32.240 --> 22:38.710
<i>to chase away all the clouds</i>

22:38.710 --> 22:49.050
<i>Your precious words are now 
fluttering through the sky</i>
